# Byte-compared vendor contract (scripts/vendor-client.mjs --check).
# These files are byte-compared against each other, so they must materialize
# with IDENTICAL bytes on every OS. Without this, a runner with
# core.autocrlf=true checks out LF-committed files as CRLF while the stamp
# literal in the LF-only script stays LF -> false "DRIFT" on Windows CI while
# Linux passes (checkout normalization). eol=lf pins the worktree bytes
# everywhere; the blobs are already LF, so this adds zero renormalization diff.
packages/knocode-client/src/client.ts text eol=lf
packages/opencode-knocode/src/vendor/** text eol=lf
packages/vscode-copilot-knocode/src/vendor/** text eol=lf

# The vendoring + version-sync scripts themselves carry template literals whose
# bytes feed those comparisons.
scripts/vendor-client.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/sync-version.mjs text eol=lf

# NOTE: PS1/other line endings are deliberately NOT managed here — the blobs are
# a pre-existing CRLF/LF mix, and touching them means a whole-file renormalization
# diff for zero behavioral gain. This file exists only to pin the byte-compared
# vendor contract above.
